      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 1:00 p.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-18-5924",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "488c33e78f0921cd2470ce7a95822f7edbc02332dc3ad51a85b1b8b9119c4f63",
      "evidence_id": "ev-488c33e78f09-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Well, what about a party that has to make decisions about how it's going to order its affairs in the wake of a decision that it wins but does it in a 4-1-4 decision? What are they -- what is that party supposed to do? Say, well, all right, we won this case, but we really can't rely on it because we don't know what -- because it has no stare decisis effect, and then what happens as the years go by and nothing happens, the Court doesn't come back to that question?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2019-18-5924",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "488c33e78f0921cd2470ce7a95822f7edbc02332dc3ad51a85b1b8b9119c4f63",
      "evidence_id": "ev-488c33e78f09-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Are you asking the Court to take up a question that five justices answered in Apodaca? That is, that the Sixth -- Apodaca, five -- there were five votes to say that the Sixth Amendment requires jury unanimity in federal trials."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "State",
      "case_id": "2019-18-5924",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "488c33e78f0921cd2470ce7a95822f7edbc02332dc3ad51a85b1b8b9119c4f63",
      "evidence_id": "ev-488c33e78f09-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It is the state's position that it would create upheaval as to the law. It would raise questions like the one the Chief Justice asked about whether seven to five is okay."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-18-5924",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "488c33e78f0921cd2470ce7a95822f7edbc02332dc3ad51a85b1b8b9119c4f63",
      "evidence_id": "ev-488c33e78f09-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Since you mentioned Balzac, can I ask you a question about that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Fisher",
      "case_id": "2019-18-5924",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "488c33e78f0921cd2470ce7a95822f7edbc02332dc3ad51a85b1b8b9119c4f63",
      "evidence_id": "ev-488c33e78f09-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think I would -- I would say that would be different for all the reasons I just outlined. The Insular Cases were majority decisions from the Court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2019-18-5924",
